WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.383 --> 00:00:01.826
- When I knew I wasn't going to college

00:00:01.826 --> 00:00:03.163
'cause I barely got out of high school.

00:00:03.163 --> 00:00:04.963
I said, "I better find
something right quick."

00:00:04.963 --> 00:00:06.209
So what am I good at?

00:00:06.209 --> 00:00:07.627
I was making people laugh.

00:00:07.627 --> 00:00:11.039
I'm busy, I'm real busy so I got to tell

00:00:11.039 --> 00:00:12.992
people like the president
of the United States,

00:00:12.992 --> 00:00:14.919
Mandela, that I can't hang out with them

00:00:14.919 --> 00:00:16.538
because I got to go loot.

00:00:16.538 --> 00:00:19.905
- First time I met him in
William Morris' office,

00:00:19.905 --> 00:00:21.838
and he just keep talking.

00:00:21.838 --> 00:00:23.289
I just look at that guy, why?

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:24.835
Why he keep talking?

00:00:24.835 --> 00:00:28.225
- Right now I'm going to
jump off a 20-story building.

00:00:28.225 --> 00:00:31.796
With no pads, I don't like
pads, they slow down the jump.

00:00:31.796 --> 00:00:34.065
So, y'know. I'm going to do it.

00:00:34.065 --> 00:00:37.345
- He's an American actor
and stand-up comedian.

00:00:37.345 --> 00:00:40.617
He's best known for his roles
as Smokey in the film "Friday"

00:00:40.617 --> 00:00:43.474
and Detective James Carter
in the "Rush Hour" series.

00:00:43.474 --> 00:00:45.719
He also became a frequent
stand-up performer

00:00:45.719 --> 00:00:48.319
on Def Comedy Jam in the 1990s.

00:00:48.319 --> 00:00:50.052
He's Chris Tucker, and here is my take

00:00:50.052 --> 00:00:51.998
on his top 10 rules of success.

00:00:51.998 --> 00:00:54.147
Rule number three is my personal
favorite, and I'm curious

00:00:54.147 --> 00:00:56.147
to figure out which one
you guys like the best.

00:00:56.147 --> 00:00:58.051
And as always, guys, as Chris is talking,

00:00:58.051 --> 00:01:00.106
if he says something that
really resonates with you,

00:01:00.106 --> 00:01:01.958
please leave it in the comments below,

00:01:01.958 --> 00:01:02.866
put quotes around it

00:01:02.866 --> 00:01:05.085
so other people can be inspired as well.

00:01:05.085 --> 00:01:05.918
Enjoy!

00:01:08.836 --> 00:01:11.586
(dramatic music)

00:01:19.088 --> 00:01:22.874
- When did you know that
you wanted to be a comedian?

00:01:22.874 --> 00:01:25.740
Like were you really
young or a little older?

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:27.131
- When I was young, I was in high school.

00:01:27.131 --> 00:01:28.753
When I knew I wasn't going to college

00:01:28.753 --> 00:01:29.952
'cause I barely got out of high school.

00:01:29.952 --> 00:01:31.662
I said, "I better find
something right quick."

00:01:31.662 --> 00:01:32.835
So what am I good at?

00:01:32.835 --> 00:01:34.778
I was making people laugh and I was like,

00:01:34.778 --> 00:01:35.674
"Why you all laughing?"

00:01:35.674 --> 00:01:37.420
"You funny! You remind
me of Eddie Murphy."

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:39.106
So I said let me try this out.

00:01:39.106 --> 00:01:40.991
And I host my talent show in high school

00:01:40.991 --> 00:01:43.359
and I got my first laugh
and I got an epiphany.

00:01:43.359 --> 00:01:45.151
And I was like, "I'm going to do this."

00:01:45.151 --> 00:01:47.356
'Cause it's fun and I'm all ready, y'know.

00:01:47.356 --> 00:01:50.521
So that's when I found out, I
hosted my first talent show.

00:01:50.521 --> 00:01:52.630
I hosted a talent show in
high school, and I said

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:53.868
that's what I want to do.

00:01:53.868 --> 00:01:55.120
- What advice would you give people,

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:58.938
based on your own experience,
about how to manage the money?

00:01:58.938 --> 00:02:00.819
- Aw man, you know what,

00:02:00.819 --> 00:02:03.894
in, you know, it's best,
invest in yourself,

00:02:03.894 --> 00:02:05.281
that's the number one thing.

00:02:05.281 --> 00:02:07.321
Don't go investing in
stuff you don't know about.

00:02:07.321 --> 00:02:09.786
'Cause nine times out of ten
you're probably going to lose it

00:02:09.786 --> 00:02:12.331
or get scammed out of it 'cause
whoever you invested with

00:02:12.331 --> 00:02:14.285
they know more about it than you.

00:02:14.285 --> 00:02:16.491
And they going to say,
"Well just let me take this

00:02:16.491 --> 00:02:17.715
if he don't know what he's doing."

00:02:17.715 --> 00:02:21.174
So invest in yourself and
try to own as much as you can

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:23.552
and save, you know, save your money,

00:02:23.552 --> 00:02:25.966
and by saving it's investing in yourself.

00:02:25.966 --> 00:02:29.674
If whatever, it's equipment
or keeping yourself healthy

00:02:29.674 --> 00:02:33.238
or whatever because you
know the longer you stay in

00:02:33.238 --> 00:02:35.788
whatever business you're
in the more likely

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:37.660
you're going to keep making money,

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:40.758
you're going to keep being relevant.

00:02:40.758 --> 00:02:43.686
I look towards the future.

00:02:43.686 --> 00:02:47.152
And the future is just, it's more to do,

00:02:47.152 --> 00:02:50.506
it's more steps to climb and stuff.

00:02:50.506 --> 00:02:53.488
So I don't really look at
what I'm doing right now

00:02:53.488 --> 00:02:55.374
I just, every time I
do something I move on

00:02:55.374 --> 00:02:57.054
and see how could I get better.

00:02:57.054 --> 00:03:00.176
And I'm never satisfied, I
always know I could do better.

00:03:00.176 --> 00:03:01.467
[Charlie Rose] - Always
knew you could do better?

00:03:01.467 --> 00:03:02.629
- I could do better, yeah.

00:03:02.629 --> 00:03:04.464
So all that stuff I
was just dreaming about

00:03:04.464 --> 00:03:07.130
like this is the
possibilities that can happen

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:09.013
if I move to California, or if, you know

00:03:09.013 --> 00:03:10.427
'cause I was working really hard here

00:03:10.427 --> 00:03:12.660
and a lot of comedians come
down from L.A. and say,

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:14.095
"Man you need to go to California

00:03:14.095 --> 00:03:15.663
'cause you're pretty good."

00:03:15.663 --> 00:03:17.003
I was getting a lot of good advice

00:03:17.003 --> 00:03:19.092
and a lot of people who
was really rooting for me.

00:03:19.092 --> 00:03:20.592
Yeah, I just went and did it,

00:03:20.592 --> 00:03:22.869
but I had a dream, and that dream

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:26.002
gave me, you know,
confidence to keep going.

00:03:26.002 --> 00:03:29.620
The power of believing
and dreaming is real.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:32.848
Because that's all I did
was dream and believe

00:03:32.848 --> 00:03:36.798
that these things could happen
and it made me feel good.

00:03:36.798 --> 00:03:38.691
And that was my, that's true wealth.

00:03:38.691 --> 00:03:40.914
If you believe and you're doing something,

00:03:40.914 --> 00:03:43.223
you have a goal, you have
a dream to get somewhere,

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:44.966
it makes you feel good.

00:03:44.966 --> 00:03:48.534
Right now I'm going to jump
off a 20 story building.

00:03:48.534 --> 00:03:50.217
With no pads, 'cause I don't like pads,

00:03:50.217 --> 00:03:52.004
they slow down the jump.

00:03:52.004 --> 00:03:55.127
So, y'know, I'm going to do it.

00:03:55.127 --> 00:03:58.544
(high-pitched screaming)

00:03:59.707 --> 00:04:02.442
It was surprising, every
day was something different

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:04.566
and it was real fun, I'm
glad he did it that way

00:04:04.566 --> 00:04:06.641
because you know you have to always,

00:04:06.641 --> 00:04:08.010
you get up in the morning

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:09.815
and you don't know what to expect.

00:04:09.815 --> 00:04:11.872
And it was a real good experience

00:04:11.872 --> 00:04:14.177
and my part was a stretch for me

00:04:14.177 --> 00:04:16.365
because I never did
anything like that before

00:04:16.365 --> 00:04:19.309
and it was so far from me and what I do

00:04:19.309 --> 00:04:22.271
in America's stand-up comedy.

00:04:22.271 --> 00:04:24.732
You know I do like reality jokes and stuff

00:04:24.732 --> 00:04:27.659
and my movies I used to do are reality,

00:04:27.659 --> 00:04:30.559
like based of America
situations and stuff,

00:04:30.559 --> 00:04:33.458
it was nothing like that.

00:04:33.458 --> 00:04:36.570
But when I got there
and Jean-Paul Gaultier,

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:38.134
I seen all his clothes
that he wanted me to wear

00:04:38.134 --> 00:04:39.465
I was like, "Oh this
ain't going to be nothing

00:04:39.465 --> 00:04:40.748
like I ever done before!"

00:04:40.748 --> 00:04:43.091
- Boy is fueled! (voice
distorts) Like fire!

00:04:43.091 --> 00:04:45.118
'Cause I would never wear
this stuff in the street.

00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:46.273
- So start melting, ladies,

00:04:46.273 --> 00:04:47.933
'cause the boy is hotter than hot!

00:04:47.933 --> 00:04:51.230
- So I was like, shit,
this going to be hard.

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:52.519
Jean-Paul Gaultier was like,

00:04:52.519 --> 00:04:54.411
(exaggerated French accent)
"This is beautiful on you!

00:04:54.411 --> 00:04:56.150
You would love this design!"

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:58.614
I was like, "No I do not like that."

00:04:58.614 --> 00:05:00.779
(normal voice) But I
start wearing the stuff

00:05:00.779 --> 00:05:03.065
and started getting into
the character and it helped,

00:05:03.065 --> 00:05:05.934
the costuming helped me
create that character a lot.

00:05:05.934 --> 00:05:09.523
I'm busy, I'm real busy, so I got to tell

00:05:09.523 --> 00:05:11.632
people like the President
of the United States,

00:05:11.632 --> 00:05:13.577
Mandela, that I can't hang out with them

00:05:13.577 --> 00:05:15.359
because I got to go loot.

00:05:15.359 --> 00:05:16.992
Oh hell no, I ain't dubbing!

00:05:16.992 --> 00:05:20.416
When I'm in a session I
always could make it better.

00:05:20.416 --> 00:05:21.524
Get your ass up!

00:05:21.524 --> 00:05:22.357
Let go!

00:05:22.357 --> 00:05:23.190
(yells)

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:25.470
I'm a perfectionist.

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:28.911
I can't stress this enough,
I am a perfectionist!

00:05:28.911 --> 00:05:31.276
- Take 55 is when Chris really shines.

00:05:31.276 --> 00:05:32.707
- 55 is the one.

00:05:32.707 --> 00:05:35.609
I like pressure because it
brings the best out of me.

00:05:35.609 --> 00:05:37.359
You got it? Let's go!

00:05:38.759 --> 00:05:40.753
I watch everything down to the last detail

00:05:40.753 --> 00:05:42.662
because I can't trust them,
I don't know how they're

00:05:42.662 --> 00:05:45.627
going to edit me, I got
to go see for myself.

00:05:45.627 --> 00:05:48.888
This is where Mark puts
Rush Hour 2 together,

00:05:48.888 --> 00:05:50.894
make it look good, make it funny

00:05:50.894 --> 00:05:52.684
if it's not funny, then I, y'know

00:05:52.684 --> 00:05:54.304
I slap him upside the back of the head.

00:05:54.304 --> 00:05:55.320
Keep it going!

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:59.174
My fans and everybody they
going to want to see the best.

00:05:59.174 --> 00:06:01.058
Got to look out for number one.

00:06:01.058 --> 00:06:04.424
I have a good partner who
started out as my manager,

00:06:04.424 --> 00:06:06.357
now we're partners.

00:06:06.357 --> 00:06:08.292
And I say that to him

00:06:08.292 --> 00:06:10.175
because I say that I learned a little bit

00:06:10.175 --> 00:06:13.206
over the three years
that I didn't do movies,

00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:16.423
I learned, I learned more about business,

00:06:16.423 --> 00:06:18.135
about the business, how it worked,

00:06:18.135 --> 00:06:20.227
and about movies and everything.

00:06:20.227 --> 00:06:22.813
So I think it's appropriate
to say we're partners

00:06:22.813 --> 00:06:24.565
because he does some of the business side

00:06:24.565 --> 00:06:27.448
and I do the acting side,
his name is Tracy Kramer.

00:06:27.448 --> 00:06:28.533
- Right

00:06:28.533 --> 00:06:30.987
- But definitely as far
as business, you know,

00:06:30.987 --> 00:06:32.655
I think he sees the
same vision that I have

00:06:32.655 --> 00:06:33.789
and where I want to go, and it's-

00:06:33.789 --> 00:06:36.967
[Charlie Rose] - Talk about that vision.

00:06:36.967 --> 00:06:39.669
Well it's a vision of
doing something different

00:06:39.669 --> 00:06:43.105
and not doing what's already been done.

00:06:43.105 --> 00:06:45.413
Because I always think, you know

00:06:45.413 --> 00:06:48.085
I'm trying to evolve as a person

00:06:48.085 --> 00:06:50.883
and also as an actor, and do great movies.

00:06:50.883 --> 00:06:53.919
I think a lot of good stories
just haven't been told yet.

00:06:53.919 --> 00:06:56.266
I think it's a lot of -

00:06:56.266 --> 00:06:59.738
movies should be, Harry
Belafonte told me this

00:06:59.738 --> 00:07:01.233
and I'll never forget it, he told me that

00:07:01.233 --> 00:07:05.466
movies should be how life
is, I mean how life should be

00:07:05.466 --> 00:07:07.149
not how life is.

00:07:07.149 --> 00:07:09.107
You know, and I always
remember that because

00:07:09.107 --> 00:07:12.820
you know, life should be
perfect, it should be good.

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:13.938
- But it's not and so,

00:07:13.938 --> 00:07:14.771
(cell phone ringing)

00:07:14.771 --> 00:07:15.690
That's you.
- I can't believe this

00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:16.756
(laughing)

00:07:16.756 --> 00:07:17.811
I cannot believe this, this
happened to me in the movies.

00:07:17.811 --> 00:07:19.302
- See who it is and we'll see
if we want to talk to them.

00:07:19.302 --> 00:07:22.123
- Yeah let's see who it is. Hello?

00:07:22.123 --> 00:07:23.825
Hey, Tracy, I just
finished talking about you,

00:07:23.825 --> 00:07:25.362
I'm on Charlie Rose show.
- Put him on.

00:07:25.362 --> 00:07:27.003
- Okay, hold on, Charlie
Rose wants to talk to you.

00:07:27.003 --> 00:07:29.634
- Tracy, this is Charlie Rose.

00:07:29.634 --> 00:07:31.872
Now I just asked him who was
responsible for his success,

00:07:31.872 --> 00:07:33.527
we didn't know you were
calling here, obviously,

00:07:33.527 --> 00:07:34.694
Where are you?

00:07:35.547 --> 00:07:38.473
In Los Angeles?! Didn't you
know he was taping this show?

00:07:38.473 --> 00:07:39.878
(Chris laughing)

00:07:39.878 --> 00:07:44.045
You did. And you know what
to expect on this show?

00:07:45.031 --> 00:07:47.013
You think Chris can handle it?

00:07:47.013 --> 00:07:49.109
Now let me just ask you this,

00:07:49.109 --> 00:07:51.492
he comes here to do the
show and so I said to him

00:07:51.492 --> 00:07:54.367
we talked about this remarkable
success, and I said to him,

00:07:54.367 --> 00:07:57.364
"Is anybody else responsible
for your success?"

00:07:57.364 --> 00:07:59.542
And he said, "Not one single soul."

00:07:59.542 --> 00:08:00.682
(laughing)

00:08:00.682 --> 00:08:04.156
He said "I got this manager
who I made a partner

00:08:04.156 --> 00:08:07.545
and I'm not sure that was a good idea."

00:08:07.545 --> 00:08:08.955
Do I have the right guy?

00:08:08.955 --> 00:08:11.254
[Voiceover] - After conceiving
the dreams to become

00:08:11.254 --> 00:08:13.372
a stand-up comedian and actor,

00:08:13.372 --> 00:08:17.388
Chris began the grind
necessary to realize them.

00:08:17.388 --> 00:08:20.163
Including working at his only job outside

00:08:20.163 --> 00:08:21.643
of the entertainment industry;

00:08:21.643 --> 00:08:24.365
his father's janitorial service.

00:08:24.365 --> 00:08:26.426
[Chris] - You know I used
to work that at night early,

00:08:26.426 --> 00:08:30.454
you know, 8 to like 11, then
I would go clean up McDonalds,

00:08:30.454 --> 00:08:33.396
Burger Kings, Kriscoll's at that time

00:08:33.396 --> 00:08:36.517
because I had the freedom cause
my dad had his own business

00:08:36.517 --> 00:08:38.954
and he taught me a lot, he
taught me how to be a businessman

00:08:38.954 --> 00:08:42.066
he taught me how to you
know, work hard, hard work,

00:08:42.066 --> 00:08:43.649
and I put that into

00:08:43.649 --> 00:08:47.640
my stand-up career and my acting career.

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:50.472
You know the lesson I've
learned just, you know,

00:08:50.472 --> 00:08:54.405
always make, you know,
friends and communicate,

00:08:54.405 --> 00:08:57.827
just don't isolate yourself
because in this business

00:08:57.827 --> 00:09:00.644
it's up and it's downs,
but the people you know

00:09:00.644 --> 00:09:03.557
and people who really know
you, they'll know who you are.

00:09:03.557 --> 00:09:04.981
Somebody says something
bad about you, it's,

00:09:04.981 --> 00:09:07.329
"Nah, he ain't like that,
I know, I really know him."

00:09:07.329 --> 00:09:09.045
So have, you know, like
in any other thing,

00:09:09.045 --> 00:09:10.420
in any other business, in school,

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:12.078
that's why people go to Harvard

00:09:12.078 --> 00:09:14.338
'cause it's the connections,
it's the people you know,

00:09:14.338 --> 00:09:17.063
and you're going to find some
good people here and there.

00:09:17.063 --> 00:09:18.481
But that's one thing I keep with me

00:09:18.481 --> 00:09:22.258
'cause you need good people
in your life and you know

00:09:22.258 --> 00:09:23.700
that's what it's about,
'cause the business is

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:26.476
always going to go up and down
you know, that's always fickle

00:09:26.476 --> 00:09:28.723
but your life is constant.

00:09:28.723 --> 00:09:29.648
[Interviewer] - Who are some of the actors

00:09:29.648 --> 00:09:32.448
that you've worked with that

00:09:32.448 --> 00:09:33.339
it became

00:09:33.339 --> 00:09:35.130
a friendship that means a lot to you,

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:39.709
or maybe it's a connection
that you have with them that

00:09:39.709 --> 00:09:42.484
professionally you like?

00:09:42.484 --> 00:09:43.317
- I think,

00:09:45.264 --> 00:09:46.700
Chris Tucker.

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:49.204
(audience applauds)

00:09:49.204 --> 00:09:51.799
Even though I don't like
him in the beginning.

00:09:51.799 --> 00:09:52.632
(laughter)

00:09:52.632 --> 00:09:55.011
- Tell us about that part.

00:09:55.011 --> 00:09:58.409
- First time I met him
in William Morris office,

00:09:58.409 --> 00:10:00.473
and he just keep talking,

00:10:00.473 --> 00:10:01.820
I just look at that guy, why?

00:10:01.820 --> 00:10:03.472
Why he keep talking?

00:10:03.472 --> 00:10:05.722
(laughter)

00:10:06.768 --> 00:10:08.850
And he's so fast!

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:10.900
Mostly people like

00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:11.734
Brett Ratner,

00:10:11.734 --> 00:10:14.077
and like my manager,

00:10:14.077 --> 00:10:18.277
(slowly) "Jackie. The movie
is really good for you."

00:10:18.277 --> 00:10:19.790
I understand, you know.

00:10:19.790 --> 00:10:23.910
And Chris Tucker: (fast gibberish)

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:25.083
I just, ugh.

00:10:25.083 --> 00:10:28.516
I just "Ah! Uh-huh! Ah! Hm! Ha ha ha!"

00:10:28.516 --> 00:10:30.865
(laughter)

00:10:30.865 --> 00:10:33.047
Then, then after he left,

00:10:33.047 --> 00:10:34.425
"Yeah, haha!"

00:10:34.425 --> 00:10:36.346
After left then I ask my manager,

00:10:36.346 --> 00:10:38.137
"What the hell he talking about?"

00:10:38.137 --> 00:10:39.288
(laughter)

00:10:39.288 --> 00:10:43.260
I don't even one word know
that come from his mouth.

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:45.613
And later on he use it in the movie.

00:10:45.613 --> 00:10:47.038
And he's too young!

00:10:47.038 --> 00:10:50.914
And too young, and comes
to the set, so many idea

00:10:50.914 --> 00:10:53.205
and he was late on the set.

00:10:53.205 --> 00:10:54.971
I was 7 o'clock call,

00:10:54.971 --> 00:10:57.329
I was 6:30, I already
in make up, standing,

00:10:57.329 --> 00:10:59.990
I'm filmmaker, standing here.

00:10:59.990 --> 00:11:02.781
Then he just comes 11 o'clock late.

00:11:02.781 --> 00:11:03.614
[Interviewer] - 11?

00:11:03.614 --> 00:11:04.529
- Yeah!

00:11:04.529 --> 00:11:06.112
Late and late.

00:11:06.112 --> 00:11:08.278
And so one day he comes to my motor home,

00:11:08.278 --> 00:11:10.890
"Jackie! Can you come later?"

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:11.988
[Interviewer] - "You're
making me look bad!"

00:11:11.988 --> 00:11:13.783
- Yeah! "You make me look bad."

00:11:13.783 --> 00:11:15.613
I said "No! That's my job."

00:11:15.613 --> 00:11:19.325
"No, you have the right to come late."

00:11:19.325 --> 00:11:20.677
[Interviewer] - Did you? Did you want to?

00:11:20.677 --> 00:11:23.701
- No! I said no, I'm a
director I can come late,

00:11:23.701 --> 00:11:26.848
when I'm an actor I have to
on the set, that's my job.

00:11:26.848 --> 00:11:28.356
But now

00:11:28.356 --> 00:11:30.523
Chris everyday on the set,

00:11:32.369 --> 00:11:35.762
and do what, just do the
really really good things.

00:11:35.762 --> 00:11:38.052
Now I really like him.

00:11:38.052 --> 00:11:42.834
But now he's just on the set
you know and follow the rules.

00:11:42.834 --> 00:11:44.867
Now he's great. Most the time he's,

00:11:44.867 --> 00:11:46.867
"Jackie! Where are you?"

00:11:48.976 --> 00:11:50.963
I said, "I'm in Hong Kong!"

00:11:50.963 --> 00:11:53.280
"Okay! When you come to United States?"

00:11:53.280 --> 00:11:54.113
I said "Coming soon!"

00:11:54.113 --> 00:11:56.019
"We can join together!"

00:11:56.019 --> 00:11:59.636
I say "Okay okay!" (air kisses)

00:11:59.636 --> 00:12:01.672
- I'm so excited to be here
and so honored to be here

00:12:01.672 --> 00:12:04.261
for my good friend, my
brother from another mother,

00:12:04.261 --> 00:12:05.392
Jackie Chan!

00:12:05.392 --> 00:12:07.640
(cheers)

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:10.887
He's one of the biggest
movie stars in the world

00:12:10.887 --> 00:12:13.203
and he has been for a long time

00:12:13.203 --> 00:12:14.774
'cause he made me one of them,

00:12:14.774 --> 00:12:16.848
all over the world. (laughs)

00:12:16.848 --> 00:12:20.348
When we did Rush Hour in, uh, ninety-eight

00:12:21.595 --> 00:12:23.802
I never seen so much love.

00:12:23.802 --> 00:12:25.881
We traveled around the
world and Jackie had

00:12:25.881 --> 00:12:28.217
these fans already coming

00:12:28.217 --> 00:12:30.884
from Asia to Australia to Europe

00:12:32.067 --> 00:12:35.768
and immediately he helped me
get known internationally.

00:12:35.768 --> 00:12:39.240
And it was just an honor
to be in a movie with him

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:43.335
and with somebody with such comic timing,

00:12:43.335 --> 00:12:45.590
comedy skills, and actions skills.

00:12:45.590 --> 00:12:48.266
That was a comedian's
dream, that was my dream,

00:12:48.266 --> 00:12:50.720
to be in a movie that I could
do whatever I wanted to do

00:12:50.720 --> 00:12:53.909
and Jackie was right there
with the right timing with me.

00:12:53.909 --> 00:12:57.132
And he's been a mentor, a big brother,

00:12:57.132 --> 00:13:00.460
he's the best guy in the whole wide world,

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:03.077
and he's just, I'm
honored to be his friend,

00:13:03.077 --> 00:13:07.177
I'm so happy to be here today
to celebrate this big day.

00:13:07.177 --> 00:13:09.575
The, uh, the first China,

00:13:09.575 --> 00:13:12.508
Chinaman-person to get an award.

00:13:12.508 --> 00:13:13.390
(laughter)

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:15.309
Did I say that right? Aw
man, I messed that up.

00:13:15.309 --> 00:13:18.654
I'm sorry! That was the character,
the Rush Hour character.

00:13:18.654 --> 00:13:19.514
I'm sorry.

00:13:19.514 --> 00:13:24.353
He's the first person from
China to get his handprint

00:13:24.353 --> 00:13:27.254
and his feet put in
here, that's what I said.

00:13:27.254 --> 00:13:28.327
(cheering)

00:13:28.327 --> 00:13:30.494
That's what you put, okay?

00:13:31.474 --> 00:13:34.997
And I love him like a brother,
and I'm happy for him,

00:13:34.997 --> 00:13:38.112
and I know you guys do too,
and I'm happy to be here.

00:13:38.112 --> 00:13:40.695
Thank you very much, thank you!

00:13:41.689 --> 00:13:43.774
- Thank you guys so much for watching,

00:13:43.774 --> 00:13:47.198
I made this video because
David Mares asked me to.

00:13:47.198 --> 00:13:48.216
So if there's a famous entrepreneur that

00:13:48.216 --> 00:13:50.745
you want me to profile next,
leave it in the comments below,

00:13:50.745 --> 00:13:52.953
and I'll see what I can do.

00:13:52.953 --> 00:13:54.282
I'd also love to know, what did

00:13:54.282 --> 00:13:55.731
Chris say that had the
biggest impact on you?

00:13:55.731 --> 00:13:57.797
What was your favorite rule from him?

00:13:57.797 --> 00:14:00.548
What message did he have that
you're going to immediately apply

00:14:00.548 --> 00:14:02.275
to your life or your business?

00:14:02.275 --> 00:14:04.943
Leave it in the comments, I'm
going to join in the discussion.

00:14:04.943 --> 00:14:07.258
Finally I wanted to give a quick
shout-out to Carolyn Owens.

00:14:07.258 --> 00:14:09.848
Carolyn, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book

00:14:09.848 --> 00:14:12.002
"Your One Word" and tweeting about it,

00:14:12.002 --> 00:14:14.516
I hope you enjoy the read,
thank you for your support.

00:14:14.516 --> 00:14:17.125
Thank you guys again for
watching, I believe in you,

00:14:17.125 --> 00:14:19.672
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:14:19.672 --> 00:14:22.749
and whatever your one word is, much love.

00:14:22.749 --> 00:14:24.249
I'll see you soon.

